{"hash":"91e1ef962272a0fc","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":74.731,"said":"Stop for a moment before this bronze. The woman seated here, her sari drawn over her head, a garland in her hands, is Punyashlok Ahilyabai Holkar, the queen who gave Vishwanath his present temple in 1780. She was born in 1725 in Chondi, a village in Maharashtra, the daughter of the village headman. Married as a child into the Holkar house of Indore, she was widowed in 1754. Her father-in-law, Malhar Rao, would not let her die on her husband’s pyre; he taught her to govern instead. From 1767 until her death in 1795 she ruled Malwa from Maheshwar on the Narmada, and her reign is remembered for its order and prosperity, and for justice that was quick, practical and kind. ‘Punyashlok’ means one whose very name is holy to speak. Her gifts to Kashi did not end with the temple: Ahilya Ghat, on the river below, still bears her name. Fold your hands to her, and then go down to the Ganga, as so many of her pilgrims did.\n\nDid you know? The statue stands on the Dham’s terrace beyond the Mandir Chowk, on the way to the river.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":923},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":939,"end":1028}],"words":[[0.098,0.409,0,4],[0.519,0.168,5,8],[0.699,0.036,9,10],[0.747,0.433,11,17],[1.192,0.409,18,24],[1.613,0.18,25,29],[1.805,0.481,30,36],[3.197,0.156,38,41],[3.365,0.349,42,47],[3.726,0.397,48,54],[4.135,0.325,55,59],[4.651,0.168,61,64],[4.832,0.373,65,69],[5.216,0.385,70,75],[5.613,0.288,76,80],[5.913,0.18,81,84],[6.106,0.312,85,89],[6.635,0.12,91,92],[6.767,0.481,93,100],[7.26,0.132,101,103],[7.404,0.144,104,107],[7.56,0.457,108,113],[8.293,0.168,115,117],[8.474,0.673,118,128],[9.159,0.613,129,138],[9.784,0.565,139,145],[10.577,0.096,147,150],[10.685,0.337,151,156],[11.034,0.12,157,160],[11.166,0.288,161,165],[11.466,0.577,166,176],[12.055,0.168,177,180],[12.236,0.433,181,188],[12.68,0.457,189,195],[13.149,1.226,196,203],[15.264,0.18,205,208],[15.457,0.204,2